Designed and implemented a 19-question, 5-level SQL analysis framework to evaluate warehouse closure decisions across utilization, product, customer, and feasibility dimensions, using MySQL (CTEs, window functions, conditional aggregation). Built a two-tier weighted scoring model to normalize and combine 19 disparate business metrics into a single, defensible closure-suitability ranking per warehouse. Conducted sensitivity analysis across 5 alternative weighting scenarios to stress-test the recommendation against different business priorities (cost, growth, customer risk). Developed and deployed an interactive Streamlit dashboard with live weight-adjustment sliders, enabling stakeholders to explore how the recommendation shifts under different assumptions
